---
// src/pages/blue-staffy-pup-sale-uk/index.astro — REBUILT from the approved board record
// (data/boards/blue-staffy-pup-sale-uk.json, approved 2026-09-20). Hand-written and NOT
// regenerated by `npm run extract`: the slug is listed in data/facts/rebuilt.json, so
// `migration_parity.py` skips it and `facts_preserved_check.py`, `link_parity_check.py` and
// `verbatim_set_check.py` are its gates instead.
//
// THIS IS THE MONEY PAGE. Four money figures and no others: £1,500 for a male, £1,700 for a
// female, a £500 refundable deposit and £200 to £350 for UK home delivery. Every one of them
// is a value in data/price-matrix.json or data/settings.json, read here rather than typed —
// the counter strip prints all four of the record's own `stats` rows, the hero's ledge prints
// the two prices, and the two tables print the record's own cells. The migrated page's £850
// to £1,200 band is nowhere on it (Known Issue 11, `dropped.prices`), and neither are the
// four unevidenced counters, the four puppy
// names, the twelve-week age or the six delivery cities — the last of which came out of the
// `sale-delivery-uk` FAQ answer too. Each is logged in the record's `dropped` with its reason.
//
// WORKING RULE 15 (faithful rewrite). The VERBATIM SET — the migrated H1, every H2/H3
// carrying a target keyword, the first paragraph under each of those headings and every
// image alt — is carried WORD FOR WORD from the migrated body at 63a7b12. Everything else is
// written fresh, in Lisa Bright's first person, from the record's outline; not one sentence
// of it is pasted. Nine deviations are recorded in the record's `verbatim.changed` with
// their reasons, and `scripts/verbatim_set_check.py --check` proves every element is
// accounted for.
//
// WORKING RULE 16. The hero is `H-FS3` and the counter strip is `C-FS1` — the for-sale
// family's own arrangements from HERO_STYLES_BY_PAGE_TYPE and COUNTER_STYLES_BY_PAGE_TYPE,
// resolved through `pickedStyle()` exactly as every other section's pick is. The hero's ledge
// is `stats`, so it prints the two PRICE rows of the record's sourced figures — the counter
// two sections down owns all four — and no trust chips and no CTA buttons (amendment 6a);
// the record's `chips` and `ticks` are handed over unchanged and the arrangement is what
// decides that they do not render.
//
// TWELVE SECTIONS, in the record's order, each mounted in the style `approval.picks` names.
// No link, image or section is here that the board does not carry. NO EMBED: the migrated
// page had none (data/facts/blue-staffy-pup-sale-uk.json — embeds empty), so none is placed.
//
// THE LISTING PAGE OWNS THE PER-PUPPY OFFERS (spec §2). This page marks the price up as ONE
// Product whose `offers` is an AggregateOffer over the litter, so the two pages never claim
// the same offer twice; the puppy grid links to /buy-blue-staffy-puppies-uk/ for the rest.
//
// H4-H6 ARE WRITTEN HERE, not in the record (amendment 2.1): the approved outline stops at
// the H3 the breeder read. Every ladder sentence traces to the migrated body or to a file
// under data/ (amendment 6f), and the H6 lines all open on the record's own
// `tuple.h6_prefixes` entry, "Price Note:". Every heading renders through `titleCase()`
// (amendment 4b) — approved wording, site-wide case.
import PageShell from '../../layouts/PageShell.astro';
import Hero from '../../components/kit/Hero.astro';
import CounterStrip from '../../components/kit/CounterStrip.astro';
import DataTable from '../../components/kit/DataTable.astro';
import PuppyCard from '../../components/kit/PuppyCard.astro';
import Testimonial from '../../components/kit/Testimonial.astro';
import ContactFormKit from '../../components/kit/ContactFormKit.astro';
import Faq from '../../components/kit/Faq.astro';
import { sectionsFromRecord } from '../../lib/sections';
import { pickedStyle } from '../../lib/pickedStyle';
import { boxClass } from '../../lib/boardStyles';
import { bakedAssets } from '../../lib/assets';
import { recordText, ledgeText, type LedgeEntry } from '../../lib/recordText';
import { titleCase as T } from '../../lib/headings';
import { loadFaq } from '../../lib/faq';
import { SITE, abs, guaranteeLabel, guaranteeCoverSentence, type PuppyRow } from '../../lib/site';
import puppiesJson from '../../../data/puppies.json';
import reviewsJson from '../../../data/reviews.json';
import prices from '../../../data/price-matrix.json';
import record from '../../../data/boards/blue-staffy-pup-sale-uk.json';

const path = '/blue-staffy-pup-sale-uk/';
// The picked meta variants and H1, BY INDEX from the approval — never retyped here.
const title = record.meta_set.titles[record.approval!.meta!.title];
const description = record.meta_set.descriptions[record.approval!.meta!.description];
const h1 = record.h1.variants[record.approval!.h1];

// The five photographs, by slot, at their ORIGINAL public paths with their ORIGINAL alt text
// (working rule 11; those five alts are also five elements of the verbatim set). A missing
// slot throws at build rather than rendering an image with no alt.
const asset = bakedAssets(record);
const heroPhoto = asset('sale-hero');
const damWithPups = asset('sale-dam-with-pups');
const deliveryVan = asset('sale-delivery');
const ownerLondon = asset('sale-owner-london');
const buyNow = asset('sale-buy-now');

// THE SIX PUPPIES, filtered on `status` rather than hard-coded: a puppy leaving the list is a
// data edit, not a page edit. All six rows are Available today — Roman, Byrd and Ince at
// £1,500 and Vennie, Christa and Cheryl at £1,700. Their card links are the grid's own data
// and are exempt from link parity (amendment 6b).
const available = (puppiesJson as PuppyRow[]).filter((p) => p.status === 'Available');

// ALL THREE REVIEWS, rendered as a grid. `approval.picks` gives this section the S1 BED, and
// the mode is the record's own note ("MODE: grid"), passed explicitly — the same split the
// homepage makes: `boxClass()` emits no mode, so the bed is the style's and the count is the
// board's. Every slot is filled, so no REVIEW_PLACEHOLDER renders here.
const allReviews = reviewsJson;

// THE FIVE FAQ ROWS THE RECORD NAMES, BY ID, in the record's order. Four of the five carry
// the migrated page's own questions word for word (rule 15); `deposit` is the fifth and its
// answer IS a setting, which is why the rows are selected by id rather than by `source`.
// `sec` is `src/lib/recordText.ts`, shared with the listing and the why-us page: a section a
// rename has removed throws with this record's slug in the message rather than handing back
// `undefined` for a `!` to wave through.
const { sec } = recordText(record);
const faqSection = sec('questions');
const faqRows = loadFaq();
const faqs = faqSection.tree.map((n) => {
  const row = faqRows.find((r) => r.id === n.heading);
  if (!row) throw new Error(`blue-staffy-pup-sale-uk: data/faq.json has no row ${n.heading}`);
  return row;
});

// The two tables, cell for cell from the record. Every figure in them is a value on disk, and
// they are the only places on this page a money figure is printed. Both stack into labelled
// rows below 640px — `DataTable` carries `.stack-table` unconditionally (working rule 13).
const priceTable = sec('prices').table!;
const deliveryTable = sec('delivery').table!;

// The hero's and the counter's own data, off the record. Nothing here is derived on the page.
const heroSection = sec('top');
// THE LEDGE STATES THE TWO PRICES, not all four figures. The hero and the counter strip sit
// one section apart and the record hands both the same four `stats` rows, so printing all
// four twice made the second strip a reprint rather than a summary. The hero takes the two
// the H1 asks about — what a puppy costs — and the deposit and the delivery band are read on
// the counter, which is the section whose whole job they are. The filter is on the recorded
// SOURCE path and not on a position, so a row inserted above one cannot change which two are
// printed, and neither figure is typed here. The record now lists the two it prints: the
// other two rows were removed in the 2026-09-21 re-approval (spec §9 amendment 11), which is
// the route a post-approval trim inside `record_hash` takes.
const PRICE_LEDGE = ['data/price-matrix.json#male_gbp', 'data/price-matrix.json#female_gbp'];
const heroStats = heroSection.stats!
  .filter((r) => typeof r.source === 'string' && PRICE_LEDGE.includes(r.source))
  .map((r) => ({ n: r.n, label: r.label }));
if (heroStats.length !== PRICE_LEDGE.length) {
  throw new Error('blue-staffy-pup-sale-uk: the record no longer carries both price stat rows');
}
const heroChips = (heroSection.hero!.chips as LedgeEntry[]).map(ledgeText);
const heroTicks = (heroSection.hero!.ticks as LedgeEntry[]).map(ledgeText);
const counterStats = sec('at-a-glance').stats!.map((r) => ({ n: r.n, label: r.label }));

const sections = sectionsFromRecord(record);

// Each section's approved arrangement, resolved through the same `boxClass()` the board
// preview called: what the breeder signed off is what ships.
const style = (id: string) => pickedStyle(record, id);
const box = (id: string) => boxClass(style(id));
const heroStyle = style('top');
const counterStyle = style('at-a-glance');

// "Mo-Su 09:00-23:00" as a sentence, from the setting rather than typed as prose.
const hours = SITE.hours.replace('Mo-Su ', 'from ').replace('-', ' to ');

// The record's schema plan: WebPage + Product + AggregateOffer + FAQPage
// (`brief.schema.types`, `offer_model: "aggregate-offer"`). WebPage comes from BaseLayout.
// The AggregateOffer's figures are data/price-matrix.json's and the count is the length of
// the same filtered list the grid renders, so the markup and the page can never disagree —
// and the per-puppy Offers stay on /buy-blue-staffy-puppies-uk/, which owns them. NO
// `availability`: an InStock claim belongs to one dog's own page (scripts/schema_check.py
// blocks it anywhere else), and a band over six puppies is a price, not a stock statement.
// The FAQPage
// node is built from the SAME five rows the accordion renders. `data/faq.json` keeps the
// sentence-case wording, which is what `name` reads; the visible question is cased at render
// (amendment 6g). No `dateModified` here on purpose — BaseLayout adds the WebPage node with
// the git-derived dates, and a second date on one page is worse than one.
const pageSchema = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'Product',
    '@id': `${abs(path)}#product`,
    name: 'Blue Staffordshire Bull Terrier puppy',
    description: 'A KC-registered blue Staffordshire Bull Terrier puppy from Blue Staffy UK, '
      + 'microchipped, vaccinated and vet-checked before it leaves us.',
    image: abs(heroPhoto.file),
    brand: { '@type': 'Brand', name: SITE.name },
    offers: {
      '@type': 'AggregateOffer',
      priceCurrency: prices.currency,
      lowPrice: String(prices.male_gbp),
      highPrice: String(prices.female_gbp),
      offerCount: String(available.length),
      url: abs(path),
    },
  },
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'FAQPage',
    '@id': `${abs(path)}#faq`,
    mainEntity: faqs.map((r) => ({
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: r.q,
      acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: r.a },
    })),
  },
];
---
<PageShell
  title={title}
  description={description}
  canonical={path}
  ogType="article"
  schema={pageSchema}
  sections={sections}
>
  {/* 01 top — hero, picked style H-FS3 (stacked on a steel band, the figures under the copy).
      No trust chips and no CTA buttons: the arrangement's ledge is `stats`, so what sits
      under the lede is the record's two PRICE rows — the deposit and the delivery band belong
      to the counter one section down, so the two strips summarise rather than repeat. The
      photograph is the migrated
      page's own primaryImageOfPage at its original path and alt. */}
  <section slot="hero" id="top" data-section-label="What a puppy costs" class={box('top')}>
    <Hero
      as="h1"
      eyebrow={`KC registered · ${SITE.location_label}`}
      title={T(h1)}
      {/* TWO LINES, because the desktop lede is `-webkit-line-clamp: 2` and a clamp HIDES its
          overflow — a third line disappears rather than pushing anything past the ceiling, so
          the defect is invisible on the page and only a measurement finds it. This one ran
          three lines at 1280 and four at 1024. Measured after: 0 overflow at 1024, 1100 and
          1280. The four money questions the sentence used to list are the four figures on the
          counter one section down, which is where a reader reads them anyway. */}
      lede="I am Lisa Bright, and this Blue Staffy pup sale UK page answers the money questions in full."
      image={heroPhoto.file}
      imageAlt={heroPhoto.alt}
      imageWidth={heroPhoto.w}
      imageHeight={heroPhoto.h}
      imageSrcset="/images/buy-staffordshire-bull-terrier-uk-now-760.webp 760w, /images/buy-staffordshire-bull-terrier-uk-now.webp 918w"
      layout={heroStyle.layout.hero ?? 'stacked'}
      align={heroStyle.layout.align ?? 'center'}
      media={heroStyle.layout.media ?? 'top'}
      ledge={heroStyle.layout.ledge ?? 'stats'}
      chips={heroChips}
      ticks={heroTicks}
      stats={heroStats}
    />
    <p>
      Every figure on this page comes from one price list, so the tables, the cards and the
      answers further down can never disagree about it. What a puppy costs, what the deposit is and whether it comes
      back, what the price already includes and what the journey home adds are all answered
      below. You can work the whole cost of getting a puppy home out here, on one screen,
      without reading the litter page or the why-us page first.
    </p>
  </section>

  {/* 02 at-a-glance — stats, picked style C-FS1 (figure cards, labels above the figures). The
      strip prints the record's four `stats` rows, each carrying the path it came from; not
      one of them is typed into this page. */}
  <section id="at-a-glance" data-section-label="The four figures, up front" class={box('at-a-glance')}>
    <div class="bl-head">
      <p class="bl-eyebrow">Read straight from our files</p>
      <h2>{T('The Four Figures, Up Front')}</h2>
      <p class="bl-lede">
        Two prices, one deposit and one delivery band. Nothing here is written by hand, so
        none of it can drift from what we charge.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="bl-body">
      <CounterStrip
        stats={counterStats}
        tiles={counterStyle.layout.tiles ?? 'card'}
        label={counterStyle.layout.label ?? 'above'}
      />
      <p>Change a figure in our price file and all four cards move with it.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* 03 why-choose — standard, picked style S1 (prose with the image right; no photograph
      here, so the prices stay above the fold on a phone). Restored under rule 15: the H2's
      opening and the "Ethical Breeding Standards" H3 and its opening are the migrated page's
      own, and only the head of the H2 moved, because the old wording collides with a live
      heading on /buy-blue-staffy-puppies-uk/ (verbatim.changed). Four sentences, one per
      pillar, and then the reader is sent to the page that argues them. */}
  <section id="why-choose" data-section-label="Why families choose a blue Staffy pup" class={box('why-choose')}>
    <div class="bl-head">
      <h2>{T('Why Families Choose a Blue Staffy Pup from BlueStaffyUK.uk')}</h2>
      <p class="bl-lede">
        Your search for a “Blue Staffy pup near me” ends with us! We pride ourselves on breeding healthy, happy, and well-socialised Staffies.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="bl-body">
      <div class="bl-prose">
        <div class="bl-stub">
          <h3>{T('Ethical Breeding Standards')}</h3>
          <p>
            Our commitment to responsible breeding means healthy parents and happy puppies, always.
          </p>
          <p>
            Maggie and Jones have both been through the DNA tests for L-2-HGA and HC-HSF4, the two
            inherited conditions a Staffordshire Bull Terrier is screened for, and their
            litters register with the Kennel Club. Each puppy is microchipped and vet checked.
          </p>
          <p>
            <a href="/buy-staffy-puppies-for-sale-uk/">The full case, reason by reason</a> is
            on the page that argues it at length, so this one can stay about the money.
            <a href="https://www.royalkennelclub.com/health-and-dog-care/health-dog-care/health/getting-started-with-health-testing-and-screening/dna-testing/dna-test-l-2hga/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The registry's own page for the L-2-HGA DNA test</a> says
            what that test looks for.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* 04 prices — table, picked style S2 (zebra rows inside a card). Every cell is the
      record's and every figure in the record is a value in data/price-matrix.json. The
      balance column is the one subtraction a reader should not have to do in their head. All
      three table styles stack into labelled rows below 640px (working rule 13). */}
  <section id="prices" data-section-label="The price of a puppy, by sex" class={box('prices')}>
    <div class="bl-head">
      <h2>{T('The Price Of A Puppy, By Sex')}</h2>
      <p class="bl-lede">
        This is the only place on the page a puppy price is written, and there are two of
        them. Sex is the one thing that moves the figure.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="bl-body">
      <DataTable
        caption={priceTable.caption}
        columns={priceTable.columns}
        rows={priceTable.rows}
        numeric={priceTable.numeric}
      />
      <h3>{T('Why The Two Prices Differ')}</h3>
      <p>
        Our price file holds one figure for a male and one for a female, and nothing else
        varies: not the colour, not the markings and not which of the two parents a puppy
        favours.
      </p>
      <h3>{T('What The Balance Is')}</h3>
      <p>
        The balance is the price less the deposit, and it is due before the puppy leaves us.
        <a href="/buy-blue-staffy-puppies-uk/">See which puppies are available at each price</a> on
        the listing page, which carries each dog by name.
      </p>
      <h4>{T('Nothing Is Added After The Table')}</h4>
      <p>
        The four columns above are the whole bill for a puppy. Only the journey home is still
        open, and the table two sections down prices it.
      </p>
      <h5>{T('Both Figures Come From One File')}</h5>
      <p>They cannot disagree with the cards above them, because they are the same values.</p>
      <h6>{T('Price Note: Tell us which puppy you mean')}</h6>
      <p>
        <a href="#enquiry">Tell us which puppy</a> in the form at the foot of this page and we
        will confirm the figure for that dog.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* 05 whats-included — standard, picked style S1 (prose with the image right), carrying the
      migrated photograph of Maggie with her pups at its original path and alt. Six items and
      no more: they are what the migrated puppy-package sentence and the `puppy-package` row
      of data/faq.json name. The health guarantee is not a seventh item: it is stated as a
      promise in the H5 below, from data/settings.json `guarantee_label` (answer board q07,
      2026-09-29). */}
  <section id="whats-included" data-section-label="What is included in the price" class={box('whats-included')}>
    <div class="bl-head">
      <h2>{T('What Is Included In The Price')}</h2>
      <p class="bl-lede">
        Six things travel with every puppy, and all six are in the price rather than added to
        it. Our {guaranteeLabel('lower')} is set out below them.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="bl-body">
      <div class="bl-prose">
        <img
          class="bl-img"
          src={damWithPups.file}
          alt={damWithPups.alt}
          width={damWithPups.w}
          height={damWithPups.h}
          srcset="/images/maggie-blue-staffy-dam-with-pups-760.webp 760w, /images/maggie-blue-staffy-dam-with-pups.webp 780w"
          sizes="(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 420px"
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
        />
        <div class="bl-stub">
          <h3>{T('Health And Vaccination')}</h3>
          <p>
            The first vaccinations and a full veterinary health check, both done before a
            puppy leaves us and both recorded on paper you take away.
            <a href="/blue-staffy-health-uk/">Read what we test for and what each test means</a> on
            the health page, which owns the DNA tests and the vaccination course.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="bl-stub">
          <h3>{T('Microchip And Paperwork')}</h3>
          <p>
            Every puppy is microchipped here, and the relevant paperwork goes with the dog on
            the day. Our lines are registered with
            <a href="https://www.royalkennelclub.com/search/breeds-a-to-z/breeds/terrier/staffordshire-bull-terrier/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">the registry our litters are registered with</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="bl-stub">
          <h3>{T('Worming And Flea Treatment')}</h3>
          <p>
            Both are done here and both are written on the paperwork, with the dates, so your
            own vet can pick the course up where we left it.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="bl-stub">
          <h3>{T('The Puppy Pack')}</h3>
          <p>
            A puppy pack goes in the car with you to make the first nights easier. It is the
            sixth item, and the list stops there.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <h4>{T('Six Items, And No Seventh')}</h4>
      <p>
        The list is the one this page has always given, and the one our FAQ gives. Nothing has
        been added to it to make the price look fuller.
      </p>
      {/* data/settings.json `guarantee_label` (answer board q07, 2026-09-29), never typed. */}
      <h5>{T(`Not an Item, a Promise: Our ${guaranteeLabel()}`)}</h5>
      <p>It is not a seventh item on the list; it is a promise we make with every puppy. {guaranteeCoverSentence()} Ask us for its full wording before you pay a deposit.</p>
      <h6>{T('Price Note: All six are inside the price')}</h6>
      <p>None of them is a line we bill for afterwards.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* 06 delivery — table, picked style S2 (zebra rows in a card), carrying the migrated
      photograph of the van at its original path and alt. The H2 is the migrated wording with
      its emoji removed and the opening is carried whole (rule 15, verbatim.changed). Two rows
      only, because two is what data/settings.json supports: no file on disk holds a distance
      band or a per-mile rate, so no city is priced here (`dropped.names`). */}
  <section id="delivery" data-section-label="Staffy puppy UK delivery" class={box('delivery')}>
    <div class="bl-head">
      <h2>{T('Staffy Puppy UK Delivery Available!')}</h2>
      <p class="bl-lede">
        Worried about location? We offer safe and reliable Staffy puppy UK delivery services! Your new family member can be transported securely to your doorstep, anywhere in the UK.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="bl-body">
      <DataTable
        caption={deliveryTable.caption}
        columns={deliveryTable.columns}
        rows={deliveryTable.rows}
        numeric={deliveryTable.numeric}
      />
      <img
        class="bl-img"
        src={deliveryVan.file}
        alt={deliveryVan.alt}
        width={deliveryVan.w}
        height={deliveryVan.h}
        srcset="/images/bluestaffyuk-nationwide-delivery-760.webp 760w, /images/bluestaffyuk-nationwide-delivery.webp 800w"
        sizes="(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 420px"
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async"
      />
      <h3>{T('Coming To Us')}</h3>
      <p>
        You are welcome to collect, and to meet the whole litter with their mother before you
        do. Collection costs nothing.
      </p>
      <h3>{T('Why The Band Is A Band')}</h3>
      <p>
        Distance is the only thing that moves the figure, and we quote yours before you commit
        to anything. Our files hold a minimum and a maximum and no per-mile rate, so we work
        it out for your address rather than reading it off a list.
      </p>
      <h4>{T('Who Carries The Puppy')}</h4>
      <p>
        Trusted DEFRA-approved transport to homes UK-wide, with the puppy's water, blanket and
        papers travelling in the crate.
        <a href="https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a819d3bed915d74e623335d/pb10308-dogs-cats-welfare-060215.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The government's welfare rules for animals in transport</a> are
        the standard behind that phrase.
      </p>
      <h5>{T('Two Rows, Because Two Is What We Hold')}</h5>
      <p>We hold a minimum and a maximum, and no price for any one destination.</p>
      <h6>{T('Price Note: Name your town in the first message')}</h6>
      <p>The band is worked out from mileage, and a town is all we need to work yours out.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* 07 deposit — standard, picked style S2 (image full width above two-column prose; no
      photograph on this record, so the two columns carry the prose alone). Prose and no
      table: the figures are in the price table one section up, and repeating them as a grid
      would be two answers to one question. */}
  <section id="deposit" data-section-label="How the deposit works" class={box('deposit')}>
    <div class="bl-head">
      <h2>{T('How The Deposit Works')}</h2>
      <p class="bl-lede">
        The deposit is refundable, and it comes off the price rather than being charged on top
        of it — which is what the balance column above already shows.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="bl-body">
      <h3>{T('What The Deposit Holds')}</h3>
      <p>
        It reserves one named puppy and takes that dog off the available list while you settle
        the rest. What it buys is that single dog, not a position on a waiting list and not a
        stake in the litter, and we will not hold a second puppy for the same household.
      </p>
      <h3>{T('Getting It Back')}</h3>
      <p>
        The deposit is refundable, and the table says so. To make a reservation, <a href="#enquiry">tell us which puppy</a> you mean, we confirm it
        is still available, and we reply within 24-48 business hours.
      </p>
      <h4>{T('Nothing Is Paid Before We Have Talked')}</h4>
      <p>
        You meet the litter first, here or on a video call. The deposit is the only commitment
        anywhere in this process.
      </p>
      <h5>{T('The Balance Is The Rest Of The Price')}</h5>
      <p>It is due before the puppy leaves us, and the table above states it for both sexes.</p>
      <h6>{T('Price Note: The deposit is not an extra')}</h6>
      <p>It is part of the price, paid earlier than the rest of it.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* 08 owners — reviews, picked style S1 (one review given room) as the BED, with the
      record's own MODE: grid passed explicitly — the same split the homepage makes. All three
      rows of data/reviews.json render, which is every real review the site holds, so no
      REVIEW_PLACEHOLDER is counted here. The two testimonials the migrated page carried are
      in `dropped.names`: neither is in any file on disk. */}
  <section id="owners" data-section-label="What families said after they paid" class={box('owners')}>
    <div class="bl-head">
      <p class="bl-eyebrow">Every review we hold</p>
      <h2>{T('What Families Said After They Paid')}</h2>
      <p class="bl-lede">
        Three families, named, on the process, the paperwork and the answering. Three is the
        number our file holds, and an invented fourth is not going to appear on it.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="bl-body">
      <Testimonial mode="grid" reviews={allReviews} />
      <img
        class="bl-img"
        src={ownerLondon.file}
        alt={ownerLondon.alt}
        width={ownerLondon.w}
        height={ownerLondon.h}
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async"
      />
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* 09 puppies — puppies, picked style S1 (three-up card grid), carrying the migrated
      photograph of the pups at its original path and alt. The heading is this page's own: the
      migrated one collided with two live pages and stated a twelve-week age no file holds
      (verbatim.changed). The opening is the migrated paragraph with the age and the old price
      band excised. The cards' own links are grid data and are exempt from link parity. */}
  <section id="puppies" data-section-label="The puppies these prices belong to" class={box('puppies')}>
    <div class="bl-head">
      <h2>{T('The Puppies These Prices Belong To')}</h2>
      <p class="bl-lede">
        Looking to purchase Staffordshire Bull Terriers in the UK? Our blue Staffy puppies are healthy, vaccinated, and ready to join your home.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="bl-body">
      <div class="bl-cards">
        {available.map((p) => <PuppyCard slug={p.slug} />)}
      </div>
      <img
        class="bl-img"
        src={buyNow.file}
        alt={buyNow.alt}
        width={buyNow.w}
        height={buyNow.h}
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async"
      />
      <p>
        The grid filters on status, so a reserved dog leaves it the same day. For
        <a href="/buy-staffy-puppies-for-sale-uk/">the reasons families choose us</a>, that is
        the page.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* 10 questions — faq, picked style S3 (accordion in a card with a jump list beside it).
      Five rows of data/faq.json: four carry the migrated accordion's questions word for word,
      because that accordion asked them as keyword H3s and they are therefore elements of this
      page's verbatim set, and the fifth is the deposit row, which data/settings.json sources.
      Each of the four answers is the migrated answer with its one unbacked clause excised, and
      every excision is recorded in the record's `verbatim.changed`. */}
  <section id="questions" data-section-label="Your questions, answered" class={box('questions')}>
    <div class="bl-head">
      <h2>{T('Your Questions, Answered: Blue Staffy Puppies FAQs')}</h2>
      <p class="bl-lede">
        Got questions about adopting your Blue Staffy puppy or our ethical breeding process? We’ve gathered the most common inquiries to help you find the answers you need quickly.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="bl-body">
      <p>
        Five rows, in the order people ask them. Four are the questions this page has been
        asked since it went up, kept word for word: how to reserve a puppy, whether our
        litters are registered and health-checked, whether we deliver, and what the price
        includes. The fifth is the deposit, at the same figure the tables give.
      </p>
      <Faq items={faqs} />
      <h4>{T('The Accordion Adds No New Claim')}</h4>
      <p>
        Open any row and you will find the sections above saying the same thing, with the same
        deposit figure the tables give.
      </p>
      <h5>{T('Send Us The Question These Miss')}</h5>
      <p>We raised these puppies, so there is a great deal more we can tell you on request.</p>
      <h6>{T('Price Note: No answer here sets a price of its own')}</h6>
      <p>The one that states the deposit gives the figure from the tables above.</p>
    </div>
    <aside class="bl-aside">
      <p class="bl-eyebrow">In this section</p>
      <ul>
        {faqs.map((r) => <li>{r.q}</li>)}
      </ul>
    </aside>
  </section>

  {/* 11 enquiry — form, picked style S1 (form under the heading). The one enquiry form on
      this page, and it is here because this is the money page: a reader who has read the
      price, the deposit and the delivery band should not have to navigate to act. The
      migrated form was a WordPress widget removed at migration (data/page-map.json
      refresh_flags wp-form-removed). ContactFormKit renders its own note and the privacy
      link; the migrated form's mobile-number line is not restated (`dropped.text`). */}
  <section id="enquiry" data-section-label="Tell us about your dream pup" class={box('enquiry')}>
    <div class="bl-head">
      <h2>{T('Tell Us About Your Dream Pup!')}</h2>
      <p class="bl-lede">
        These beautiful Blue Staffordshire Bull Terrier puppies for sale are seeking loving homes. Don’t miss the chance to welcome a Blue Staffy into your family!
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="bl-body">
      <p>
        Three things make a message easy to answer: the puppy you have your eye on, the town
        you are writing from, and who shares the house with you. With those, the reply can
        settle everything at once.
      </p>
      <ContactFormKit />
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* 12 talk-to-us — standard, no pick recorded: prose is prose. The close, and the calmest
      thing a money page can say — come and look before you pay anything. No countdown and no
      scarcity: the migrated page's "won't last long" line is in `dropped.text`, because the
      buying guide tells a reader to treat sales pressure as a warning sign. */}
  <section id="talk-to-us" data-section-label="Come and see them first">
    <h2>{T('Come And See Them First')}</h2>
    <p>
      Come and meet the litter before you decide anything. The puppies are still with their
      mother here in the house, and you are welcome to sit with them. Not everybody likes a
      form: write to {SITE.email} instead if you would rather, and we look {hours} every day.
    </p>

    <h3>{T('Visits Are By Appointment')}</h3>
    <p>
      This is a family home rather than a kennel with a reception, so we fix a time between
      us first and one of us is here to open the door.
      <a href="/uk-blue-staffy-breeders-contact/">Write to us to arrange a visit</a> if you
      would rather start on the contact page.
    </p>

    <h3>{T('What To Put In A First Message')}</h3>
    <p>
      The puppy's name, the town you are in and who is in the household.
      <a href="/uk-blue-staffy-puppy-buying-guide/">Put our buying-guide questions to us before you decide</a>.
    </p>
    <h4>{T('We Have No Number To Give You Yet')}</h4>
    <p>
      Until one is provisioned, this site prints no telephone number rather than a wrong
      one. Email gets to us, and the reply comes within 24-48 business hours.
    </p>
    <h5>{T('Meet Maggie Before You Pay Anything')}</h5>
    <p>Watching a dam with her own litter answers more than any paragraph on this page can.</p>
    <h6>{T('Price Note: Nothing is due before a visit')}</h6>
    <p>The deposit comes after you have met the puppy, never before.</p>
  </section>
</PageShell>
